# Global saved emotions

When a user adds a **custom emotion** (via "Other — type your own") anywhere in Ledger, it must be remembered **for that user** on every form that reports emotions.

## Storage

- Server: `user_preferences.saved_emotions` via `GET/PUT /api/preferences` (`static/ledger_prefs.js`)
- Client cache / offline fallback: `localStorage` key `ledger_saved_emotions`
- On first load, empty server prefs import from localStorage once, then sync both ways
- All emotion pickers must use `emotion_wheel_picker` + `LedgerPrefs` — do not invent alternate keys

## Behavior

- Custom emotions are saved automatically when used — no opt-in checkbox
- Built-in wheel emotions are never duplicated into saved storage
- Saved emotions appear in the **Saved** category on every picker (check-in, diary card extras, thought record, etc.)
- Removing a saved emotion from one picker removes it for that user everywhere
- Pickers listen for `ledger-saved-emotions-changed` and `storage` events to stay in sync

## When adding emotion UI

- Reuse `templates/macros/emotion_wheel.html` and `static/ledger_prefs.js`
- Do not introduce alternate keys or browser-only custom emotion lists for picker UI
